{title: He Brought Me Out Of The Miry Clay}
{key: C}
{x_theme: grace-mercy, praise, faith-trust}
{x_source: chrd:he_brought_me_out_of_the_miry_clay.chrd}

{comment: Chorus}
[C]He Bro't Me Out Of The Miry Clay,
[G]He Set My Feet On The Rock To Stay,
[C]He   [F]Puts A Song In My Soul Today,
[C]A    [G]So- n[C]g Of   Praise, Halle-lu-jah.

{comment: Verse 1}
[C]My Heart Was Distressed 'Neath Jehovah's Dread Frown,
[F]A -  [C]n - d [G]Low In The Pit Where My Sins Dragged Me Down;
[C]I    [F]Cried To The Lord From The Deep Miry Clay,
[C]W -h- [G]o    [C]Tenderly Bro't Me Out To Golden Day.

{comment: Verse 2}
[C]He Placed Me Upon The Strong Rock By His Side,
[F]M -  [C]y    [G]Steps Were E-stablished And Here I'll A-bide;
[C]No   [F]Danger Of Falling While Here I Remain,
[C]B -u- [G]t    [C]Stand By His Grace Until The Crown I Gain.

{comment: Verse 3}
[C]He Gave Me A Song, 'Twas A New Song Of Praise,
[F]B -  [C]y    [G]Day And By Night Its Sweet Notes I Will Raise,
[C]My   [F]Heart's Over Flowing, I'm Happy And Free,
[C]I -'- [G]ll   [C]Praise My Redeemer, Who Has Rescued Me.
